Yeah it's called Vi or Vim (Vi iMproved), and it's the only way to edit
text on a terminal.  (None of this Emacs/Pico stuff!)

Here is a quick ref that might help you:
http://www.vim.org/tips/tip.php?tip_id=422

Vi/Vim is probably one of the most popular console editors, and most
people comfortable with consoles (i.e. the kind of people who would be
playing on NAO, or even playing Nethack for that matter) are familiar
with it.  I agree with you, it might be a bit more "user friendly" if
they defaulted to Pico, but remind me: since when was anything about
Nethack user friendly?  :-P



